<title>USA: Clinton proposes to extend oil spill excise tax.</title>
<headline>Clinton proposes to extend oil spill excise tax.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Clinton administration Thursday proposed to extend the 5 cents a barrel excise tax on U.S. crude oil and imported crude and petroleum products in the 1998 fiscal year to help fill the Oil Spill Liability Trust Fund.</p>
<p>The tax is expected to yield $200 million a year from 1998 through 2002, and would be suspended during any quarter when the trust fund in the preceding quarter held more than $2.5 billion.</p>
</text>
